// Cars on ring roads after Nagel and Schreckenberg
// (examples/traffic/ring.ent). Without braking every road settles within
// the warm-up to a flow of exactly min(density * vmax, 1 - density) cars
// a step, so over 400 steps its cars move min(cars * vmax, cells - cars)
// cells a step, and no step is off. The draws to brake are worked out from
// the seed, the car and the step, so the run is the same on one core and
// on all of them. (examples/traffic/check/flow.py holds the flows of a
// whole sweep against the exact formulas.)
// RUN: %ent run -I %S/../../examples/traffic %S/Inputs/traffic_ring.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.one
// RUN: %ent run --parallel -I %S/../../examples/traffic %S/Inputs/traffic_ring.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.all
// RUN: cmp %t.one %t.all
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.one

// vmax 1 is rule 184: free below half the cells, jammed above.
// CHECK:      vmax 1 brake 0.0 cars 160 moved 64000 of 400 steps, off 0
// CHECK-NEXT: vmax 1 brake 0.0 cars 180 moved 72000 of 400 steps, off 0
// CHECK-NEXT: vmax 1 brake 0.0 cars 200 moved 80000 of 400 steps, off 0
// CHECK-NEXT: vmax 1 brake 0.0 cars 220 moved 72000 of 400 steps, off 0
// With vmax 5 the flow is highest at a sixth of the cells.
// CHECK-NEXT: vmax 5 brake 0.0 cars 40 moved 80000 of 400 steps, off 0
// CHECK-NEXT: vmax 5 brake 0.0 cars 80 moved 128000 of 400 steps, off 0
// CHECK-NEXT: vmax 5 brake 0.0 cars 120 moved 112000 of 400 steps, off 0
// CHECK-NEXT: vmax 5 brake 0.0 cars 160 moved 96000 of 400 steps, off 0
// Braking at random: about 0.146 * 400 cells * 400 steps.
// CHECK-NEXT: vmax 1 brake 0.5 cars 200 moved {{2[34][0-9][0-9][0-9]}} of 400 steps, off 0
